  "summary": "Black-lacquer boxes painted with fairytale villages in icon-painter gold — icons reborn as miniature worlds.",
  "description": "When Soviet iconoclasm ended Palekh's icon trade, its master painters turned their hand to papier-mâché boxes, inventing a new genre in 1922-25: scenes from folklore, song and Pushkin rendered in tempera so fine that figures fit under a fingernail, glowing against deep black lacquer with gold-leaf highlighting in the old icon manner. Elongated figures, rhythmic hills, firebird reds and fine gold assist lines made Palekh instantly distinct from Fedoskino realism. The Palekh school still trains painters through a decade-long apprenticeship.",
